<div class="modal fade" id="police4Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="police4ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable" style="max-width:800px;">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
          <img src="{{ asset('images/Layer1.png') }}" alt="National Police (HQ)" style="width:24px; height:24px; object-fit:contain;">
          <h5 class="modal-title" id="police4ModalLabel">National Police (HQ)</h5>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
      </div>

      <div class="modal-body">
        <p><strong>Command Level:</strong> Highest active uniformed operational command</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Head Rank:</strong> Commissioner of Police (CP)</p>
        <p><strong>Role:</strong> Executive head of the Marshall Islands Police Department (MIPD), managing day-to-day operations, personnel discipline, and public safety enforcement nationwide.</p>
        <p>The Police Commissioner exercises overall command, supervision, and direction of all sworn officers and operational units within the MIPD. Headquartered in Majuro, the Commissioner oversees the effective enforcement of national criminal statutes, public order maintenance, border and maritime security operations, and traffic regulations throughout the archipelago&#8217;s atolls. Supported by an Assistant Commissioner who oversees administration and logistics, the Commissioner establishes departmental procedures, directs criminal investigations, heads the INTERPOL National Central Bureau (NCB) in Majuro, and reports directly to the Minister of Justice, Immigration, and Labor on police deployment, resource allocation, and national security matters.</p>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Direct national law enforcement strategies, public safety policies, and operational priorities across all island jurisdictions.</li>
          <li>Administer overall departmental budget allocations, operational expenditures, and resource management in coordination with the MOJIL.</li>
          <li>Enforce standards for officer conduct, disciplinary procedures, and internal accountability measures across the sworn ranks.</li>
          <li>Coordinate national maritime security, Exclusive Economic Zone (EEZ) surveillance, and sea patrol operations with regional and international partners.</li>
          <li>Oversee major criminal investigations, specialized police operations, and emergency response activities during national crises.</li>
          <li>Lead international law enforcement cooperation, intelligence exchange, and joint task force actions through the INTERPOL National Central Bureau (NCB) in Majuro.</li>
          <li>Authorize executive appointments, rank promotions, unit assignments, and strategic personnel transfers within the police force.</li>
          <li>Advise the Minister of Justice, Immigration, and Labor on legislative updates, internal security threats, and national policing requirements.</li>
          <li>Represent the MIPD at regional police conferences, including the Pacific Islands Chiefs of Police (PICP) association.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="modal fade" id="police3Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="police3ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable" style="max-width:800px;">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
          <img src="{{ asset('images/Layer2.png') }}" alt="Regional Police Substation" style="width:24px; height:24px; object-fit:contain;">
          <h5 class="modal-title" id="police3ModalLabel">Regional Police Substation</h5>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
      </div>

      <div class="modal-body">
        <p><strong>Command Level:</strong> Regional executive commands/major island divisions</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Head Rank:</strong> Police Sergeant (Sgt.) &#8212; Assistant Commissioner of Police (ACP).</p>
        <p>The Ebeye Sub-Station is headed by an Assistant Commissioner of Police (ACP), the Laura and Jaluit Sub-Stations are headed by Police Lieutenants (Lts.), while the Wotje Sub-Station is headed by a Police Sergeant (Sgt.).</p>
        <p><strong>Administrative Equivalent:</strong> Regional district headquarters</p>
        <p><strong>Role:</strong> Primary national police field posts responsible for extending national law enforcement, felony investigations, traffic regulation, and emergency response across regional atolls and sector zones outside Majuro Central HQ.</p>
        <p><strong>Function:</strong> MIPD Sub-Stations execute national statutory mandates, preserve public order, and manage round-the-clock emergency dispatch across designated outer-island and sector jurisdictions. Functioning as decentralized arms of the national police force, these stations conduct preliminary and felony criminal inquiries, enforce national motor vehicle statutes, manage local holding cells, and maintain maritime coastal surveillance while providing tactical backup to local municipal authorities.</p>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Maintain continuous 24/7 uniformed shift patrols, desk dispatch, and rapid emergency call response within assigned regional sectors.</li>
          <li>Conduct preliminary and felony criminal investigations, securing crime scenes for handover to CID detectives or the Attorney General&#8217;s Office.</li>
          <li>Execute national traffic law enforcement, compliance road checks, DUI interdictions, and motor vehicle registration processing.</li>
          <li>Deploy coastal patrol craft for localized maritime surveillance, EEZ monitoring support, and marine search-and-rescue missions.</li>
          <li>Serve judicial warrants, court subpoenas, and formal legal notices issued by the Judiciary for outer-island residents.</li>
          <li>Manage station holding cell blocks, ensuring secure temporary detainment and prisoner welfare before transfer to Majuro Central Jail.</li>
          <li>Sustain continuous HF/VHF radio communications, operational blotter logging, and daily incident transmissions to Majuro Central Headquarters.</li>
          <li>Coordinate joint public safety details, major event crowd control, and emergency disaster responses with local municipal leadership.</li>
          <li>Compile and submit monthly regional crime statistics, station inventory audits, and operational output reports to executive command in Majuro.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="modal fade" id="police2Modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="police2ModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable" style="max-width:800px;">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
          <img src="{{ asset('images/Layer3.png') }}" alt="Municipal Police Posts" style="width:24px; height:24px; object-fit:contain;">
          <h5 class="modal-title" id="police2ModalLabel">Municipal Police Posts</h5>
        </div>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
      </div>

      <div class="modal-body">
        <p><strong>Command Level:</strong> Municipal local government peace officer posts/autonomous local police commands</p>
        <p><strong>Typical Head Rank:</strong> Chief of Municipal Police/Municipal Police Captain</p>
        <p><strong>Administrative Equivalent:</strong> Municipal police station/local ordinance enforcement division</p>
        <p><strong>Role:</strong> Local government peace officer entities established under the Local Government Act 1980 to enforce municipal ordinances, maintain neighborhood public order, and manage localized community safety within Majuro (MALGov) and Kwajalein (KALGov).</p>
        <p>MALGov PD and KALGov PD execute localized peace officer duties under the overall legal jurisdiction and operational oversight of the MIPD. Unlike the MIPD&#8212;which holds exclusive statutory authority over national criminal code enforcement, felony investigations, traffic administration, corrections, and maritime surveillance&#8212;municipal police forces are specifically restricted to enforcing local council ordinances, managing municipal night curfews, resolving minor civil/neighborhood disputes, conducting street-level foot patrols, and regulating municipal business/waste compliance.</p>
        <p class="mb-2"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Uphold municipal council ordinances, local business licensing regulations, public health orders, and environmental waste bylaws.</li>
          <li>Conduct routine neighborhood foot beats, residential street patrols, and public order maintenance across local municipal zones.</li>
          <li>Enforce municipal night curfews for minors and commercial establishments on Ebeye and Majuro.</li>
          <li>Provide localized traffic direction, pedestrian crossing security near school zones, and parking enforcement on municipal roads.</li>
          <li>Manage static security and crowd control during local council meetings, municipal elections, civic parades, and community festivities.</li>
          <li>Perform initial intervention and de-escalation in minor neighborhood disturbances, noise complaints, and non-felony civil disputes.</li>
          <li>Detain municipal ordinance violators and hand over felony suspects or major crime scenes immediately to the national MIPD.</li>
          <li>Collaborate in joint community policing initiatives, neighborhood watch programs, and youth outreach with MIPD Community Policing teams.</li>
          <li>Maintain municipal incident blotters and transmit daily activity summaries to local municipal councils and MIPD sector supervisors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
